  "raw": {
    "https://www.timeshighereducation.com/unijobs/listing/416444/associate-lecturer-in-education-early-childhood-education-and-care-primary-/": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer in Education (Early Childhood Education and Care/Primary)",
      "description": "Associate Lecturer in Education (Early Childhood Education and Care/Primary) job with SOUTHERN CROSS UNIVERSITY | 416444 Skip to main content News Rankings Jobs Study abroad Events Resources Solutions Skip to main menu Skip to user menu Jobseekers: Login Sign up Employers: Login (This link will open in a new window) Post a\n                          job (This link will open in a new window) Employers Jobs Home Find a job Job alerts Upload CV Careers advice the.com (This link will open in a new window) More Results Associate Lecturer in Education (Early Childhood Education and Care/Primary) Employer SOUTHERN CROSS UNIVERSITY Location Coffs Harbour / Gold Coast / Lismore, Australia Salary $83,458 - $112,174 per annum, plus 17% employer’s contribution to superannuation Closing date 2 Nov 2026 View more categories View less categories Academic Discipline Education , Social Sciences Job Type Academic Posts , Lecturers / Assistant Professors Contract Type Permanent Hours Full Time Apply on website Save job Click to add the job to your shortlist You need to sign in or create an account to save a job. Send job Job Details Shape initial teacher education through innovative teaching and curriculum design Join a collaborative Faculty with a strong education research community Full-time continuing role with a choice of campus location Be Bold. Belong. Be More. At Southern Cross University, we do things differently, and so can you. A career with us is more than you might expect. Yes, it’s about the heart, connectedness and community you’d hope for in a regional university. But there’s also so much more. Our game changing Southern Cross Model brings a deeper, focused learning experience and our research is deeply connected to our regions, making a difference on a global scale. This is your chance to help us build something new and meaningful for our students, our communities and your career. To drive change, make a real impact, and thrive in a place as unique as you. You can be good anywhere. Here, you can be great. Your opportunity Southern Cross University’s Faculty of Education is seeking an Associate Lecturer in Education to contribute to the teaching, learning and research profile of the Faculty. You’ll support the development of future educators through student-centred teaching, innovative curriculum design and scholarship that enhances the student learning experience. You will make an impact by: Delivering engaging, student-centred teaching across face-to-face, blended and online modes, using contemporary learning technologies and flexible approaches. Contributing to innovative curriculum development, teaching resources and practices that enhance student learning. Undertaking research and teaching scholarship, contributing to publications, grant applications and collaborative research aligned with Faculty priorities. Building professional and community connections and contributing to Faculty activities, projects and academic service. What you will bring You’re an enthusiastic and developing academic with a passion for initial teacher education and a commitment to creating engaging, inclusive learning experiences. You bring contemporary teaching knowledge, an interest in innovative curriculum design and a developing research or teaching scholarship profile. You enjoy collaborating with colleagues and engaging with students, professional networks and the wider community. To succeed in this role, you will also need: A PhD/Professional Doctorate (or demonstrated significant progress towards completion of) in Education or relevant discipline, in addition to an initial teacher education degree Demonstrated experience in innovative university teaching and curriculum design in initial teacher education. A developing research and teaching scholarship profile, including publications, grant applications and, where applicable, research supervision. Strong communication and collaboration skills, with a commitment to cultural diversity, equity and workplace health and safety. Why Southern Cross University SCU is proudly a regional university, young, small and vibrant. That means you’ll find more exposure, opportunity and ownership - to grow, achieve and build a career that means more. And you’ll do it alongside passionate people and leaders who go the extra mile to help you succeed. A career with us is about more than just work. It’s about place, community and the life you want to live. With three main campuses at the Gold Coast , Coffs Harbour and the Northern Rivers region of NSW, we’re integral to all these wonderful communities. Find your place and be more in this beautiful part of the world. Your opportunity is: Full-time, continuing (permanent) Located at either Coffs Harbour, NSW 2450, Gold Coast, QLD 4225, or Lismore, NSW 2480. Relocation assistance is available, making it easier to join our regional communities. ACAD Level A (Associate Lecturer). The base salary ranges from $83,458 - $112,174 per annum, plus 17% employer’s contribution to superannuation. The total remuneration package is up to $131,244. You will enjoy a range of perks designed to support your wellbeing, growth and work-life balance. For more information on our benefits and what it’s like to work at SCU, visit Why work at Southern Cross University? Be more with Southern Cross University today Southern Cross University values potential as much as experience. If you do not meet all the listed requirements but are excited about the role and confident you can contribute, we encourage you to apply or reach out for more information. Name: Professor Wendy Boyd Chair of Early Childhood Education, Faculty of Education Phone: 0413 105 636 Email: wendy.boyd@scu.edu.au Applications close 11.30pm AEDT 2 November 2026 Eligible applicants must have Australian or New Zealand citizenship, Australian permanent residency or current working rights in Australia for the entire duration of the appointment. Employer visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must apply online and attach a CV and cover letter. The cover letter must clearly address each selection criterion in the position description. Information to support you prepare your application is available on our website. Southern Cross University celebrates the rich diversity of our regions and international community. We are committed to creating an inclusive workplace that welcomes and values people of all backgrounds. We encourage applications from people of all genders, ethnicities, ages, languages, sexual orientations, and people with disabilities. We are dedicated to providing reasonable adjustments to our recruitment process to ensure every candidate can fully participate. For any support through the recruitment process, reach out to jobs@scu.edu.au. #LI-AM1 #All Position description How to apply: Start your application by clicking the \"begin\" button. Login to an existing account or reset your password Preview Application Form By choosing to continue, you agree to the Privacy Notice. Show Privacy Notice Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Apply on website Send job Apply on website Save job Click to add the job to your shortlist You need to sign in or create an account to save a job. Get job alerts Create a job alert and receive personalised job recommendations straight to your inbox. Create alert Similar jobs Lecturer in Sport and Exercise Psychology Birmingham, United Kingdom Lecturer in Primary English Camperdown, Australia Post Doctoral Researcher, National Centre for Inclusive Higher Edu Maynooth, Ireland back to top Facebook (This link will open in a new window) Twitter (This link will open in a new window) LinkedIn (This link will open in a new window) Contact us Terms & Conditions Privacy Policy © 2015 - 2026 THE World Universities Insights Limited. Powered by Madgex Job Board Software Close Before you apply - Turn on alerts for jobs like this! We'll send them straight to your inbox : What is your email address? required When you create this job alert we will email you a selection of jobs matching your criteria. Our terms and conditions and privacy policy apply to this service and you can unsubscribe at any time. By clicking to continue to apply below, your email address will be shared with the employer. No thanks, continue to apply (This will open in a new window from which you will be automatically redirected to an external site after 5 seconds) Create alert and continue to apply (This will open in a new window from which you will be automatically redirected to an external site after 5 seconds) Madgex Design System Icon. Madgex Design System Icon."
