    "https://www.timeshighereducation.com/unijobs/listing/416831/senior-lecturer-in-occupational-therapy/": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer in Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer in Occupational Therapy job with SOUTHERN CROSS UNIVERSITY | 416831 Skip to main content News Rankings Jobs Study abroad Events Resources Solutions Skip to main menu Skip to user menu Jobseekers: Login Sign up Employers: Login (This link will open in a new window) Post a\n                          job (This link will open in a new window) Employers Jobs Home Find a job Job alerts Upload CV Careers advice the.com (This link will open in a new window) More Results Senior Lecturer in Occupational Therapy Employer SOUTHERN CROSS UNIVERSITY Location Gold Coast, Australia Salary $139,568 - $160,473 per annum, plus 17% employer’s contribution to superannuation Closing date 17 Nov 2026 View more categories View less categories Academic Discipline Clinical, Pre-clinical & Health , Other Health & Social Care Job Type Academic Posts , Principal / Senior Lecturers / Associate Professors Contract Type Permanent Hours Full Time Apply on website Save job Click to add the job to your shortlist You need to sign in or create an account to save a job. Send job Job Details Deliver Occupational Therapy programs at Southern Cross University Make an impact through research, scholarship and industry engagement Build your career at our vibrant beachside Gold Coast Campus Be Bold. Belong. Be More. At Southern Cross University, we do things differently, and so can you. A career with us is more than you might expect. Yes, it’s about the heart, connectedness and community you’d hope for in a regional university. But there’s also so much more. Our game changing Southern Cross Model brings a deeper, focused learning experience and our research is deeply connected to our regions, making a difference on a global scale. This is your chance to help us build something new and meaningful for our students, our communities and your career. To drive change, make a real impact, and thrive in a place as unique as you. You can be good anywhere. Here, you can be great. Your opportunity Southern Cross University’s Faculty of Health is seeking an experienced Senior Lecturer in Occupational Therapy to contribute to our new Master of Occupational Therapy program. You’ll bring your academic and clinical expertise to design contemporary teaching, strengthen research and scholarship, and prepare graduates for meaningful careers in the profession. You will join an established team of occupational therapy academics and may also teach within our Bachelor program. Depending on experience, interests and operational requirements, there may also be an opportunity to undertake leadership responsibilities through the role of Course Coordinator for the Master of Occupational Therapy. You will make an impact by: Providing academic leadership in student-centred teaching, curriculum development and innovative learning across face-to-face, blended and online environments. Advancing research and scholarship through high-quality publications, research collaborations, grant activity and scholarship of teaching. Strengthening industry and professional partnerships to enhance student learning, and contribute to the Faculty’s profile. Contributing to academic leadership and course development, with the potential opportunity to take on Course Coordinator responsibilities. What you will bring You’re an experienced occupational therapy academic who combines clinical expertise with a passion for teaching, research and advancing the profession. You enjoy collaborating with colleagues and industry partners to create contemporary learning experiences that prepare graduates for practice. To succeed in this role, you will also need: A PhD qualification, a minimum of five years’ academic and clinical experience, and registration or eligibility for registration as an Occupational Therapist with Ahpra with no conditions that would limit the capacity to fulfil the requirements of the position. Demonstrated experience teaching practical and theoretical Occupational Therapy topics using contemporary educational technologies across face-to-face, blended and online environments. Proven experience in curriculum design and evaluation, alongside a track record of research and scholarship demonstrated through publications and research grant activity. Highly developed interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to collaborate with colleagues and research partners, engage with diverse stakeholders, and demonstrate a commitment to cultural diversity, equity and workplace health and safety. Why Southern Cross University SCU is proudly a regional university, young, small and vibrant. That means you’ll find more exposure, opportunity and ownership - to grow, achieve and build a career that means more. And you’ll do it alongside passionate people and leaders who go the extra mile to help you succeed. A career with us is about more than just work. It’s about place, community and the life you want to live. With three main campuses at the Gold Coast , Coffs Harbour and the Northern Rivers region of NSW, we’re integral to all these wonderful communities. Find your place and be more in this beautiful part of the world. Your opportunity is: Full-time, continuing (permanent) Located at Gold Coast, QLD 4225. Relocation assistance is available, making it easier to join our regional communities. ACAD Level C. The base salary ranges from $139,568 - $160,473 per annum, plus 17% employer’s contribution to superannuation. The total remuneration package is up to $187,753. You will enjoy a range of perks designed to support your wellbeing, growth and work-life balance. For more information on our benefits and what it’s like to work at SCU, visit Why work at Southern Cross University? Be more with Southern Cross University today Southern Cross University values potential as much as experience. If you do not meet all the listed requirements but are excited about the role and confident you can contribute, we encourage you to apply or reach out for more information. Name: Dr Michelle Bissett, Chair of Discipline (Allied Health & Community Welfare) Phone: 0407 388 215 Email: michelle.bissett@scu.edu.au Applications close 11.30pm AEDT 17 November 2026 Eligible applicants must have Australian or New Zealand citizenship, Australian permanent residency or current working rights in Australia for the entire duration of the appointment. Employer visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must apply online and attach a CV and cover letter. The cover letter must clearly address each selection criterion in the position description. Information to support you prepare your application is available on our website. Southern Cross University celebrates the rich diversity of our regions and international community. We are committed to creating an inclusive workplace that welcomes and values people of all backgrounds. We encourage applications from people of all genders, ethnicities, ages, languages, sexual orientations, and people with disabilities. We are dedicated to providing reasonable adjustments to our recruitment process to ensure every candidate can fully participate. For any support through the recruitment process, reach out to jobs@scu.edu.au. #LI-AM1 #GC Position description How to apply: Start your application by clicking the \"begin\" button. Login to an existing account or reset your password Preview Application Form By choosing to continue, you agree to the Privacy Notice. Show Privacy Notice Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Apply on website Send job Apply on website Save job Click to add the job to your shortlist You need to sign in or create an account to save a job. Get job alerts Create a job alert and receive personalised job recommendations straight to your inbox. Create alert Similar jobs Research Assistant Adelaide, Australia Lecturer in Occupational Therapy Gold Coast, Australia Associate / Full Professor, Public Health Michigan, United States back to top Facebook (This link will open in a new window) Twitter (This link will open in a new window) LinkedIn (This link will open in a new window) Contact us Terms & Conditions Privacy Policy © 2015 - 2026 THE World Universities Insights Limited. Powered by Madgex Job Board Software Close Before you apply - Turn on alerts for jobs like this! We'll send them straight to your inbox : What is your email address? required When you create this job alert we will email you a selection of jobs matching your criteria. Our terms and conditions and privacy policy apply to this service and you can unsubscribe at any time. By clicking to continue to apply below, your email address will be shared with the employer. No thanks, continue to apply (This will open in a new window from which you will be automatically redirected to an external site after 5 seconds) Create alert and continue to apply (This will open in a new window from which you will be automatically redirected to an external site after 5 seconds) Madgex Design System Icon. Madgex Design System Icon."
